{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794511098,"nonce":"Zm6bMOhEzE/d7ZEKANzvAVIHNlE=","title":"wasm direct: no static devirtualization without a profile","message":"The LLVM wasm build devirtualized a method call in two ways: from a `--pgo` profile, and, with no profile, from a reachability analysis of the classes the program allocates (`devirt::ReachableTargets`), when a slot has at most two implementations, guarding on the loaded slot and calling directly on a match. The direct backend has the first (9865812c, `Program::method_targets`) and not the second, so a wasm build with no profile calls every method through the table.\n\nPlan: have `BytecodeProgram::method_targets` also return the analysis's targets when the profile names none, behind the same `ASH_AOT_NO_STATIC_DEVIRT` switch as the native path. It is measured, not assumed: a dispatch-heavy program (deltablue) in Chrome and wasmtime, plus module size, before it is on by default. The guarded direct call is what lets V8 inline.","files":null}]}